{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been feeling really nauseous and vomiting again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. It started this morning—really intense nausea and I’ve been vomiting green stuff."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Bilious vomiting. That’s consistent with your gastroparesis. You were just discharged two days ago—were you tolerating food then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, small sips and crackers. I even ate a banana yesterday. But today it all came back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’re not able to keep any pills down either?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not even the Zofran or Reglan. I tried this morning but threw it up right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll give you IV fluids and anti-nausea meds to start. We also need to check your blood sugar and electrolytes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My blood sugar’s usually okay with my Lantus at night. But I haven’t eaten, so it might be low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor that closely. Also, I see you have a history of breathing problems with Ativan—anything over 0.25 mg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I had apnea once in the ER after 1 mg. I only take half a tablet now if I must."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2197-06-05 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll avoid IV Ativan and be very cautious with dosing. For now, we’re giving Zofran IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your sodium dropped to 128 yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I’ve had low sodium before when I’m sick like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s likely due to SIADH from severe nausea. We’ve stopped IV fluids and put you on fluid restriction to help it rise safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can’t drink much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for now. We’ll recheck your sodium today and tomorrow. It’s already up to 131 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My stomach still feels full, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re still attributing that to gastroparesis. Gastroenterology wants to do an endoscopy to make sure there’s no other issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? I had one a few months ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2197-06-06 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but your symptoms are worsening and frequent. We need to rule out new problems like a blockage or worsening esophagitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2197-06-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood and urine cultures came back negative. No infection found."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2197-06-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a fever the first night—was that just from being dehydrated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2197-06-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your temperature was actually low at one point—95.6. But your white count was high, so we checked for infection. It looks like stress from nausea caused the changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2197-06-07 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2197-06-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not needed. Your vitals and labs are improving as your nausea settles."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2197-06-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray yesterday. Your lungs are clear, which supports that your low sodium is from SIADH, not a lung issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2197-06-08 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I saw something about a catheter in the report?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2197-06-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your port is visible, and the line is in good position. That’s how we’ve been giving your meds and drawing labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2197-06-09 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi. You just got back from your endoscopy. Everything looked okay in the stomach, but you do have esophagitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2197-06-09 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Inflammation in the esophagus? Could that be making me nauseous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2197-06-09 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can contribute, but it’s not the main cause. The good news is no ulcers or blockages. Biopsies confirmed mild inflammation, likely from reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2197-06-09 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2197-06-09 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on Protonix twice a day to treat the esophagitis. And we’re increasing your erythromycin to three times a day to help with stomach emptying."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2197-06-09 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought erythromycin was an antibiotic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2197-06-09 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "At low doses, it acts as a stomach stimulant. It’s commonly used for gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2197-06-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sodium is now 134—back in a safe range. We’re lifting the fluid restriction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2197-06-10 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! Can I start eating again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2197-06-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re starting you on clear liquids. If you tolerate that, we’ll advance to solids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2197-06-10 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your gastric pacer was adjusted this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2197-06-10 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help? It hasn’t been changed in months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2197-06-10 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The GI team thought it might need optimization. Since the adjustment, you’ve had less nausea and kept down apple juice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2197-06-10 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do feel a bit better. Less bloated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2197-06-10 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure has been running high—around 160s over 90. We’ve been giving labetalol IV since you couldn’t take pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2197-06-10 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take lisinopril and a clonidine patch at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2197-06-10 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve restarted your lisinopril and increased it to 10 mg daily. The clonidine patch was discontinued—it can worsen nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2197-06-10 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2197-06-10 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s a known side effect. We’ll monitor your BP. You’ll need a blood test—chem-7—before seeing your PCP next week to check your potassium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. You’re tolerating solid food, your sodium is stable, and your BP is in the 130s over 80."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll go home on your regular insulin, Reglan, Zofran, and compazine suppositories. Erythromycin three times a day and Protonix twice daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Ativan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can take half a tablet as needed, but be cautious. If you feel drowsy or short of breath, stop and call us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have my GI appointment tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with Dr. ___ to review the pacer settings and your progress. And see your PCP next week for BP follow-up and the blood test."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if this happens again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you can’t keep fluids down for more than 12 hours, or have dizziness, chest pain, or trouble breathing, come back to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I’ll try to stick to small meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. And keep using your anti-nausea meds early. We’re discharging you in stable condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad this round wasn’t as bad as the last one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We caught it early, adjusted your pacer, and treated the esophagitis. That should help prevent frequent admissions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so. Ten times in three months is too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re working on it. Take care, and call if anything concerns you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will go over your prescriptions and discharge instructions now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll wait for her."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing much better. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2197-06-11 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2197-06-05 10:57:00",
    "admission_end": "2197-06-11 14:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and gastroparesis s/p gastric pacer was readmitted for severe nausea and bilious vomiting, just two days after a prior discharge. She was unable to tolerate oral intake or medications. Initial management included IV fluids and antiemetics, but hyponatremia developed, reaching a nadir of 128, attributed to SIADH from prolonged vomiting; this resolved with fluid restriction. Blood and urine cultures were negative, and leukocytosis was deemed stress-related. A chest X-ray showed no pulmonary cause for hyponatremia. An upper endoscopy revealed acute esophagitis, with no gastric abnormalities. Her gastric pacer was readjusted, leading to symptom improvement and tolerance of solid foods. Hypertension persisted during admission, prompting an increase in lisinopril to 10 mg daily and discontinuation of the clonidine patch due to its nausea-inducing side effects. She was discharged home in stable condition on optimized antiemetic and acid-suppression therapy, with follow-up scheduled for pacer evaluation and primary care management of blood pressure.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Other disorders of neurohypophysis",
      "Dehydration",
      "Acute esophagitis",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other specified anemias"
    ]
  }
}
